       "id": "CVE-2026-41001",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-41001: Insecure Temporary File"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-41001?s=github&n=spring-boot-autoconfigure&ns=org.springframework.boot&t=maven&vr=%3E%3D3.5.0%2C%3C%3D3.5.14",
       "help": {
        "text": "Spring Boot's ArtemisEmbeddedConfigurationFactory uses a fixed, static path for the embedded Artemis message broker's data directory when no explicit path is configured. A local attacker on the same host can pre-create this predictable directory or place a symlink before the application starts.\n\nAffected versions:\nSpring Boot 4.0.0 through 4.0.6; 3.5.0 through 3.5.14; 3.4.0 through 3.4.16; 3.3.0 through 3.3.19; 2.7.0 through 2.7.33.\n",
        "markdown": "> Spring Boot's ArtemisEmbeddedConfigurationFactory uses a fixed, static path for the embedded Artemis message broker's data directory when no explicit path is configured. A local attacker on the same host can pre-create this predictable directory or place a symlink before the application starts.\n\nAffected versions:\nSpring Boot 4.0.0 through 4.0.6; 3.5.0 through 3.5.14; 3.4.0 through 3.4.16; 3.3.0 through 3.3.19; 2.7.0 through 2.7.33.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                    |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:maven/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot-autoconfigure@3.5.13  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=3.5.0,<=3.5.14                                                     |\n|Fixed version                                                                  3.5.15                                                               |\n|[[CVSS Score 5.3] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L]]                                                                       |\n"
       },
