       "id": "CVE-2026-59898",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-59898: Inconsistent Interpretation of HTTP Requests ('HTTP Request/Response Smuggling')"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-59898?s=github&n=netty-codec-http&ns=io.netty&t=maven&vr=%3C4.1.136.Final",
       "help": {
        "text": "## Summary\nAn attacker can force WebSocket upgrade via the lax V07 (or V08) handshaker by sending `Sec-WebSocket-Version: 7` and omitting `Connection: Upgrade` / `Upgrade: websocket` headers, completing a protocol switch that a proxy would not recognize as an Upgrade request and enabling HTTP request smuggling / protocol-confusion attacks.\n",
        "markdown": "> ## Summary\nAn attacker can force WebSocket upgrade via the lax V07 (or V08) handshaker by sending `Sec-WebSocket-Version: 7` and omitting `Connection: Upgrade` / `Upgrade: websocket` headers, completing a protocol switch that a proxy would not recognize as an Upgrade request and enabling HTTP request smuggling / protocol-confusion attacks.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                     |\n|Package                                                                                           pkg:maven/io.netty/netty-codec-http@4.1.132.Final  |\n|Affected range                                                                                    <4.1.136.Final                                     |\n|Fixed version                                                                                     4.1.136.Final                                      |\n|[[CVSS Score 6.3] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N]]                                                     |\n"
       },
