       "id": "CVE-2026-56745",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-56745: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56745?s=github&n=netty-codec-http&ns=io.netty&t=maven&vr=%3E%3D4.1.0.Final%2C%3C%3D4.1.135.Final",
       "help": {
        "text": "The `SpdyHttpDecoder` handler in Netty's SPDY-to-HTTP codec allocates a pooled `ByteBuf` when processing a client-initiated `SYN_STREAM` frame with `FLAG_FIN=0`, storing the partially-constructed `FullHttpRequest` in an internal map (`messageMap`) to accumulate subsequent `DATA` frames. When the remote peer sends an `RST_STREAM` for that stream, or when the accumulated content exceeds `maxContentLength`, the decoder removes the entry from the map but **never releases the pooled ByteBuf**, permanently leaking the allocated memory.\n",
        "markdown": "> The `SpdyHttpDecoder` handler in Netty's SPDY-to-HTTP codec allocates a pooled `ByteBuf` when processing a client-initiated `SYN_STREAM` frame with `FLAG_FIN=0`, storing the partially-constructed `FullHttpRequest` in an internal map (`messageMap`) to accumulate subsequent `DATA` frames. When the remote peer sends an `RST_STREAM` for that stream, or when the accumulated content exceeds `maxContentLength`, the decoder removes the entry from the map but **never releases the pooled ByteBuf**, permanently leaking the allocated memory.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                     |\n|Package                                                                                           pkg:maven/io.netty/netty-codec-http@4.1.132.Final  |\n|Affected range                                                                                    >=4.1.0.Final,<=4.1.135.Final                      |\n|Fixed version                                                                                     4.1.136.Final                                      |\n|[[CVSS Score 8.7] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N]]                                                     |\n"
       },
       "properties": {
