       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-59901?s=github&n=netty-codec&ns=io.netty&t=maven&vr=%3C4.1.136.Final",
       "help": {
        "text": "The `Bzip2Decoder` handler in Netty's compression codec pipeline is vulnerable to a denial-of-service attack through a malformed bzip2 stream that permanently captures the event-loop thread in an infinite loop. The vulnerability exists in the run-length encoding (RLE) state machine within [`Bzip2BlockDecompressor.read()`]\n",
        "markdown": "> The `Bzip2Decoder` handler in Netty's compression codec pipeline is vulnerable to a denial-of-service attack through a malformed bzip2 stream that permanently captures the event-loop thread in an infinite loop. The vulnerability exists in the run-length encoding (RLE) state machine within [`Bzip2BlockDecompressor.read()`]\n\n|                                                                                                                                                |\n|Package                                                                                           pkg:maven/io.netty/netty-codec@4.1.132.Final  |\n|Affected range                                                                                    <4.1.136.Final                                |\n|Fixed version                                                                                     4.1.136.Final                                 |\n|[[CVSS Score 8.7] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N]]                                                |\n"
